# M0.4 — Virtual-atom compatibility (spec §1.4). THE go/no-go for keeping
#         `drive_method = virtual_atom` with MLIPs and D3.
#
# Mechanism under test: the virtual drive atom has no chemical element, which
# `pair_style mace` cannot NULL-map and `dispersion/d3` cannot accept. Instead
# we (a) map it to a PLACEHOLDER element that exists in the model, and
# (b) remove every pair involving it from all neighbour lists. An atom with an
# empty neighbour list contributes only its constant isolated-atom energy.
#
# Geometry: bilayer_plus_virtual.data from make_geometries.py — 25 atoms,
# 5 atom types. It is byte-for-byte the M0.3 bilayer (same cell, same 24
# positions) plus one extra atom, which is what makes the constant-offset
# comparison below meaningful.
# TYPE LAYOUT:
#   1 = Mo layer 1   2 = S layer 1
#   3 = Mo layer 2   4 = S layer 2
#   5 = virtual drive atom (no element; mapped to placeholder Mo below)
#
# `neigh_modify exclude type i j` takes two explicit type numbers — there is no
# wildcard form — so the exclusions are enumerated 5-1 ... 5-5.
#
# Run:  $PREFIX/lammps-mace/build/lmp -k on g 1 -sf kk -in m0_4_virtual_exclude.in
#
# Repeat this deck with deepmd (`pair_style deepmd frozen_model.pth`,
# `pair_coeff * * Mo S Mo S Mo`) and with the dispersion/d3 overlay from M0.3b
# (adding ` Mo` to the d3 coeff line) — all three must pass.

units metal
atom_style atomic
read_data bilayer_plus_virtual.data     # type 5 = virtual atom, no neighbors wanted
pair_style mace no_domain_decomposition
pair_coeff * * mace mace.model-lammps.pt Mo S Mo S Mo   # virtual type mapped to placeholder Mo
# Masses are also in the data file; repeated here so the deck is self-contained.
mass 1 95.95   # Mo
mass 2 32.06   # S
mass 3 95.95   # Mo
mass 4 32.06   # S
mass 5 1.0     # virtual drive atom
neigh_modify exclude type 5 1
neigh_modify exclude type 5 2
neigh_modify exclude type 5 3
neigh_modify exclude type 5 4
neigh_modify exclude type 5 5
# PASS criteria (runbook): potential energy differs from the no-virtual run by a
# CONSTANT (isolated-atom energy); per-atom force on type 5 == 0; repeat deck with
# deepmd and with dispersion/d3 overlay.
group virtual type 5
compute fvirt virtual reduce maxabs fx fy fz
thermo 1
thermo_style custom step pe etotal c_fvirt[1] c_fvirt[2] c_fvirt[3]
run 0
fix nve all nve
run 20
